  "slug": "states-chiral-hoti-98d5",
  "summary": "Recent preprints recast accidental BIC existence in terms of radiation-source parity and spatially nonlocal scattering response.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the characterization of bound states in the continuum (BICs), modes that remain confined despite lying within the radiation continuum of open photonic systems. Two preprints address accidental BICs directly: one shows that in vertically asymmetric photonic lattices they are governed by radiation-source parity and can be recovered through parity restoration, while the other models metasurface BICs as converging reflection and transmission zeros and concludes that accidental BICs require spatially nonlocal response. A third preprint studies Berry phase and topological quasi-bound states in Möbius resonators, reporting a phase that depends on the mode. The fourth item, a microwave study of higher-order topological hinge states in an all-dielectric woodpile photonic crystal, shares the topological photonic context but is less directly tied to the BIC framing. The new element is the expression of accidental BIC existence in terms of parity and nonlocality.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
